A("## 3. Boundaries\n")
A("Two independent methods were run on every segment start and end (1,892 sides, 1,024 unique boundaries):\n")
A("1. **Change points.** `ruptures.KernelCPD` (linear kernel) on robust-standardised 5-frame window means of [P, M, Φ_rad±, d log R/dt]. The penalty is bisected so that the number of change points is 0.5×, 1× or 2× the number of annotated boundaries, at 3 smoothings (5, 15, 31 frames): 9 configs per dataset.")
A("2. **Label criterion crossing.** The frame nearest the boundary (±3 s) where the label's own criterion crosses its midpoint: P = 0.5 (tpol), M = 0.5 (milling), max(P,M) = 0.5 (shoaling), or the sign of d log R/dt (exp/comp). Computed at 3 smoothings. Transition segments borrow the criterion of the stable neighbour that shares the boundary.\n")
A(f"Status: *supported* = either method within ±0.5 s (the annotation grid is 0.5 s: 99.5% of timestamps fall on .0/.5). *shift_suggested* = both methods agree on a shift >0.5 s (to within 0.5 s); the suggestion is their mean. *shift_possible* = only one method is consistent. *unclear* = neither.\n")
A(f"- Segment sides: {b.status.value_counts().to_dict()}.")
