A("- Large one-frame steps above max(10× median step, 99.9th pct): in the 30/70-fish datasets almost all are backed by the velocity column, so they are real fast moves (startles). **Teleports** (velocity does not support the step) cluster in the 10-fish datasets (51–53 each in 0066/0105/0126), consistent with identity swaps or re-acquisition.")
A("- Group-level order parameters are permutation-invariant, so identity swaps barely move them. Teleports cause one-frame spikes in R and hull. All 12 annotated exp/comp segments that overlap a teleport still pass outlier-robust checks (median distance to centroid and per-fish radial velocity), so **none of the annotated expansion/compaction is a tracking artefact**.")
A("- `150_fish/0200` has **151** tracks. Group splitting (more than one cluster) is common in 0120 (24% of frames) and 0084/0107 (~10%). Splits inflate R and can look like expansion; segments with >30% split frames are noted in the CSV.\n")
